package secretstoretest // import "github.com/abigotado/agent-clis/core/secretstore/secretstoretest"

Package secretstoretest provides an in-memory secretstore.Store for tests and
Contract, a behaviour suite every secretstore.Store implementation must pass.

FUNCTIONS

func Contract(t *testing.T, s secretstore.Store, maxSecretBytes int)
    Contract runs the behaviour suite against s, which must have been opened
    with MaxSecretBytes equal to maxSecretBytes (at least 256). It stores
    only under a random service named secretstore-test-<random> and deletes
    everything it created when t finishes, so it is safe against a real store,
    though the real-backend tests of a later change run it in disposable
    environments.

    The rows are: missing keys, round trip and copy isolation, overwrite,
    idempotent delete, isolation between keys, the size bound (a value of
    exactly the bound, and one byte more leaving the previous value intact),
    empty secrets, all 256 byte values, non-ASCII accounts, accounts that differ
    only by case, accounts with wildcard characters, invalid keys on every
    operation, pre-canceled contexts, and a redaction check: a random marker
    secret, account and service never appear in provoked errors formatted with
    %v, %+v, %#v and %s, nor in slog text and JSON output.


TYPES

type Memory struct {
	// Has unexported fields.
}
    Memory is a goroutine-safe in-memory store. It validates keys and sizes
    the way the real stores do, copies secrets on the way in and out, compares
    keys case-sensitively, and can be made to fail per operation with SetErr.
    It implements secretstore.Store and secretstore.ACLRepairer.

func NewMemory(opts secretstore.Options) *Memory
    NewMemory returns an empty store. Options are checked like secretstore.Open
    checks them; with invalid options every operation fails with
    secretstore.ErrInvalidArgument instead of NewMemory panicking.

func (m *Memory) Delete(ctx context.Context, key secretstore.Key) error
    Delete implements secretstore.Store. Deleting a missing item succeeds.

func (m *Memory) Exists(ctx context.Context, key secretstore.Key) (bool, error)
    Exists implements secretstore.Store.

func (m *Memory) Load(ctx context.Context, key secretstore.Key) ([]byte, error)
    Load implements secretstore.Store. The returned slice is a copy.

func (m *Memory) RepairAccess(ctx context.Context, key secretstore.Key) error
    RepairAccess implements secretstore.ACLRepairer. Like the macOS store
    it refuses with ErrInteractionRequired unless the store was opened with
    InteractionAllowed, and it reports ErrNotFound for a missing item. Access
    control does not exist in memory, so a successful repair changes nothing.

func (m *Memory) Save(ctx context.Context, key secretstore.Key, secret []byte) error
    Save implements secretstore.Store. The store keeps a copy of secret.

func (m *Memory) SetErr(op Op, err error)
    SetErr makes op return err, after the checks that run before a real store is
    touched (context, key, size). A nil err clears it. An unknown op is ignored.

type Op int
    Op names a Memory operation for SetErr.

const (
	OpExists Op = iota
	OpLoad
	OpSave
	OpDelete
	OpRepair
)
    The operations an error can be injected into.

func (o Op) String() string
    String returns the operation name used in secretstore.Error.Op.

